# "ESP32-C6 802.15.4" profile settings file for Wireshark.
#
# Selects this profile automatically for an 802.15.4 capture -- Zigbee,
# Thread or Matter -- from any board this project supports.
#
# Selection is by RADIO, not by board. The filter names the dissector these
# columns read their values from, so the profile follows what is being sniffed
# rather than which hardware sniffed it. Any board this project gains is
# covered the day it captures, with nothing to remember.
#
# It was a list of interface names until the nRF54L15 arrived and was left off
# it. The failure mode is quiet, which is what makes it worth avoiding: the
# capture dissects perfectly and the only symptom is Wireshark's default
# columns, so channel, RSSI and LQI sit in every frame and show in none.
#
# Exclusivity is kept, which was the reason for naming interfaces in the first
# place. Measured across one capture from each radio, every filter below
# matches its own and neither of the others.
#
# wpan is the 802.15.4 dissector; the columns read the wpan-tap header it
# sits above, which has no filterable protocol name of its own.

# Automatically switch to this profile if this display filter matches
auto_switch_filter: wpan
